You’ve spent years learning how to perform under constraint. I’d be interested in discovering what happens when you bring that same capacity for learning to play, where the objective isn’t to control more but to access more.

I don’t think we need to give you a bigger engine. I think we need to find out which activities make you stop holding the brakes.